ugh flipping the state would require a shift well beyond a normal cycle.", "confidence": "medium", "notes": ["No expert ratings published yet; forecast rests on fundamentals and polls.", "New or vacant seat with no expert ratings; fundamentals only.", "No usable general-election polls; forecast rests on fundamentals and expert ratings."]}, "overview": "North Dakota remains one of the most Republican-leaning states in presidential politics, with a partisan lean of roughly 18 points toward the GOP. No incumbent is on the ballot in this open race, and no public polls, expert ratings, or prediction-market prices are available to refine the picture. The forecast therefore rests on the state's fundamental partisan balance.\n\nWith no evidence pointing to a Democratic breakthrough, the race is rated Safe Republican. An 18-point structural advantage has historically been beyond the reach of even strong national Democratic years in North Dakota, and nothing in the current picture suggests this cycle will differ. The main source of uncertainty is the national environment, which could move the margin a few points in either direction without changing the likely outcome.", "history": [{"date": "2026-09-23", "p_dem": 0.0273, "margin": -18.0}, {"date": "2026-09-24", "p_dem": 0.0558, "margin": -18.0}, {"date": "2026-09-25", "p_dem": 0.0549, "margin": -18.0}, {"date": "2026-09-26", "p_dem": 0.0572, "margin": -18.0}, {"date": "2026-09-27", "p_dem": 0.0505, "margin": -18.0}, {"date": "2026-09-28", "p_dem": 0.0515, "margin": -18.0}, {"date": "2026-09-29", "p_dem": 0.0556, "margin": -18.0}, {"date": "2026-09-30", "p_dem": 0.0598, "margin": -18.0}, {"date": "2026-10-01", "p_dem": 0.0528, "margin": -18.0}, {"date": "2026-10-02", "p_dem": 0.0566, "margin": -18.0}, {"date": "2026-10-03", "p_dem": 0.05, "margin": -18.0}, {"date": "2026-10-04", "p_dem": 0.052, "margin": -18.0}, {"date": "2026-10-05", "p_dem": 0.0544, "margin": -18.0}]}